     {
+        // PGXP shadows one PgxpValue per RAM word, so it has to be sized from the
+        // same array the guest sees. Upstream sizes it from its ctor's ramSize
+        // argument; this pin has no such argument -- the RAM is a field initializer
+        // -- so the length is read back off it here. A stale entry cannot lie: every
